  "task1_recompute_from_build_records": {
    "method_note": "Build A's day_clustered_t (all-fills and all 20 cells) reproduces exactly using the UNWEIGHTED per-day-mean t-test: per day compute R_d = sum_pnl_contract/contracts for that day, then mean/(sd/sqrt(n_days)), df=n_days-1 -- this is U1's own day_clustered_t formula (every day weighted equally regardless of volume). Build B's day_clustered_t reproduces exactly using the CONTRACT-WEIGHTED combined ratio-estimator: R_hat=sum(S_d)/sum(W_d), e_d=S_d-R_hat*W_d, Var=(n/(n-1))*sum(e_d^2)/sum(W_d)^2, t=R_hat/SE -- this is what the frozen spec's ev_accounting text literally specifies ('cluster-robust ratio-estimator SE on per-day (sum weighted P&L, sum weights)'). FLAG: A and B use two DIFFERENT, non-equivalent day-clustered t statistics on data that (for all-fills) largely overlaps in the U1-timeband region. Both reproduce their own numbers exactly from their own cached aggregates (0 mismatches in independent recompute of all-fills + all 20 cells for each build), but only B's formula matches the frozen spec's literal text; A's matches U1's own precedent formula instead. This is a real methodology divergence between the two builds, not previously flagged, though it does not change either build's own stated verdict (both are INSUFFICIENT on sanity anchor (b) regardless of which t formula is used).",
